build/
build-docs/
*.ll
*.dSYM

# Compiled binaries
website
main

# TLS certificates (generated locally)
certs/

# Logs
logs/

# NOTE (134.30): content/docs/ is NOT ignored. It is a build INPUT — `ooke
# build` renders every /docs/<section>/<slug> page from it — and it used to be
# excluded here as "local content symlinks", which left zero entries tracked and
# no documentation source at all in a fresh clone. It is now a generated, tracked
# copy; scripts/sync_docs_content.sh is the only thing that writes it.
#
# Everything ignored in this file is build OUTPUT, reproducible in a fresh clone
# by `make` and `make build`, or a local secret:
#   build/ build-docs/  rendered by scripts/build_static.sh + `ooke build`
#   website main main.ll *.ll  compiled from main.tk by `make`
#   certs/              self-signed dev certificates, made by `make certs`
#   logs/ test-results/ runtime and test-run output
# If a rule here ever covers something the build READS, that is the 127.85 /
# 134.21 / 134.30 defect again — track the file instead of widening the rule.

# macOS
.DS_Store
test-results/
